WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.870
Are human races biologically real?

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.753
Genetics says the picture is

3
00:00:04.753 --> 00:00:06.369
more complicated.

4
00:00:06.729 --> 00:00:07.503
In 1950,

5
00:00:07.503 --> 00:00:09.958
UNESCO issued its first statement

6
00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:10.903
on race.

7
00:00:10.903 --> 00:00:11.794
In 1972,

8
00:00:11.794 --> 00:00:15.086
Richard Lewontin measured where genetic

9
00:00:15.086 --> 00:00:16.892
variation lies.

10
00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:18.989
He found about 85 percent

11
00:00:18.989 --> 00:00:21.060
of genetic variation is within

12
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.529
populations, and only a small

13
00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:26.056
share between so-called races.

14
00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:28.007
Traits like skin colour change

15
00:00:28.007 --> 00:00:29.530
gradually across space.

16
00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.951
Anthropologists call these clines.

17
00:00:31.951 --> 00:00:35.379
Racism has no biological basis.

18
00:00:36.074 --> 00:00:37.245
Your turn.

19
00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:39.667
Where does most variation lie?
